-- HTB deliberate change: language and BHDStudio (package 2 of the 2026-10-19 profile review).
--
-- Approved by Steven on 2026-10-19 (items E1 and B2, and the English-dub decision).
--   - E1 "Foreign Language Only", movies only, -999,999 in every profile: the release name carries an
--     explicit language tag after the year (TRUEFRENCH, POLISH, iTALiAN and similar, not a cut name
--     like "JAPANESE CUT"), it isn't dual audio, MULTi or a language-plus-DL pair, and Radarr finds
--     no original-language audio. Replaces upstream's "Not Original or English" ban, which misfires
--     on this library's language tags. TV is left alone: episode titles contain words like "German".
--   - B2: the Balanced-tier 4K encodes (BHDStudio, HONE, hallowed, dkore) drop from about 440,000 to
--     385,000, 384,000 and 383,000 in 2160p Quality and 2160p Quality (Prefer Theatrical). Only 4K
--     WEB-DLs and Tier 6 encodes move above them.
--   - "2160p Quality (English Dub)", a Radarr profile for English-dubbed films (mostly anime). A copy of
--     2160p Quality after B2 and E1, with these differences:
--       - 4K, 1080p and 720p share one quality group, so scores decide between them.
--       - English audio is required: "English Audio Missing" bans a release with no English language,
--         and no "Dual Audio" or "DUBBED" in its name.
--       - Bonuses: Resolution 1080p +2,000,000, Resolution 2160p +4,000,000, Dual Audio +6,000,000.
--         Dual audio beats English-only at any resolution; within the same audio, 4K beats 1080p
--         beats 720p. Every other score keeps its usual meaning inside each band.
--       - Bans are -20,000,000 here, because the bonuses reach about 10,500,000 and a -999,999
--         ban would no longer win. Upgrade-until is 88,888,888 for the same reason.
--       - "Not Original" (-1) isn't scored: these films are wanted in English.
--     Upstream's "Dual Audio" and "DUBBED" formats are copied as they are (item C13).

-- E1: foreign-language guard, movies only.

-- B2: Balanced-tier 4K encodes below 4K WEB-DLs and Tier 6 encodes in the Quality profiles.

-- Upstream formats used by the English-dub profile (C13).

-- HTB formats for the English-dub profile.

